{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391759-let-s-populate-the-british-isles","id":1391759,"title":"Let's populate the British isles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-26T13:08:13-07:00","id":1391759,"title":"Let's populate the British isles","content":"One thing I have always wanted is a supplement detailing the British isles for mage the ascension. It is a topic I have seen come up numerous times so I am clearly not alone. <br /> <br /> We are unlikely to get anything official any time soon, so why not apply some group think? That way the next time anyone wants information on mage for the British isles they will have some inspiration to draw on. <br /> <br /> it seems to me that there are a number of initial strands that need consideration.<br /> <br /> Places of interest; what places in the UK would have the most interest for mages? What local legends might capture enlightened minds?<br /> <br /> Demographics; Looking at the demographics on Anders mage page (because they look pretty reasonable as a starting place for me), the isles should have about 4 chantries. Maybe 5 if two are small. And the same number of technocratic constructs.<br /> I figure probably 3 chantries across England, another across Scotland and possibly the very north of england, and the last in Ireland.<br /> Chantries have 3-5 cabals of 3-5 images each, with an average total of 15 mages in the chantry. Constructs are smaller.<br /> Two of the chantries should probably control powerful enough nodes to have a horizon realm.<br /> there should be a number of images floating around without direct chantry membership as well.<br /> <br /> Where would you place the chantries? Where would you place their nodes and other interests?<br /> <br /> Factions; the Chorus, Hermetics, and Verbena all have traditional stakes in britain. But other factions have interests there as well. <br /> <br /> what factions would you populate the UK with? How would they fill out the membership of the various chantries? Would you make any of the chantries mono tradition, or all mixed?<br /> <br /> Throw me your thoughts...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T13:49:17-07:00","id":1391770,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/168\" target=\"_blank\">Isle of the Mighty</a> is a Changeling supplement, but includes a fair amount of Mage material as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T16:04:22-07:00","id":1391802,"title":"","content":"I believe an update to <i>Isle of the Mighty</i> would be an excellent work, especially if it's Mage-focused.<br /> <br /> Given the Aided are a canon Euthanatos faction of Celtic 'death mages,' they'd also be present. Scotland has a lot of education and many famous inventors, so I'd expect some Technocracy presence there. The Nephandi, well that would bring in the Hellfire clubs and other sorts (also some more extreme Cult of Ecstasy members who have yet to Fall).<br /> <br /> Also, I recommend anyone who is doing more than spitballing look at <i>Ascension's Landscape</i> on the Storyteller's Vault. Ander's Mage page was awesome (glad to see it somewhat back on the web). <i>Ascension's Landscape</i> goes into a lot more thought about the setting implications of various population demographics and choices in Mage and has worked examples, so this would be good to use to make a plausible and useful British Isles guidebook for Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T16:52:48-07:00","id":1391806,"title":"","content":"Cause of a game I'm preparing I have a special interest in British Hollow Ones. Canon places a couple of the craft's chantries in England. Two in London, another one outside it.<br /> In the revised Order of Hermes book they also mention the tradition has a school in London.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T13:54:34-07:00","id":1392039,"title":"","content":"Thanks.<br /> I have read those books some time ago but will revisit them.<br /> I didn't realise quite how much mage stuff isle of the mighty had scattered around it pages.<br /> <br /> I also seem to have miss calculated - according to Anders demographics the UK should have around 9 chantries, hosting around 135 mages, with another 45 mages floating around unattached to any chantries, giving around 180 tradition mages in total. <br /> I whil look at how the information from isle of the mighty maps onto that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T14:07:05-07:00","id":1392044,"title":"","content":"Well, keep in mind that the demographics on Ander's Mage page, which Paul F. Strack wrote up, went with very Eurocentric demographics due to the lack of information on places outside of North American and Europe. If you go with a less Eurocentric assumption, such as the current M20 Technocracy Reloaded does by saying there are 3 Asian Technocrats to 1 European Technocrat, thus reflecting that the number of Awakened in the world is less Eurocentric, you'd have different numbers.<br /> <br /> That's where <i>Ascension's Landscape</i> comes in. What's the rate of Awakening in a culture? How lethal is the early stages of Awakening and how long do mages live (so, if you go with mages by their Arete and sphere ranks, what's the population structure from Apprentice to Oracle?). There are some worked examples of those assumptions. I'd suggest being upfront about your assumptions. While some people will question every assumption, Mage players know the world is based on them. So, if your numbers match your assumptions and make an interesting source on the British Isles, that's a good place to go.<br /> <br /> Terry Robinson's fellow podcaster at Mage: the Podcast interviewed Paul Strack about Ander's Mage Page and Paul's work there. The podcast is a good listen, especially if you were checking out that page in the 1990s. . .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://magethepodcast.com/index.php/2019/05/25/interview-with-paul-strack/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://magethepodcast.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/cropped-test.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://magethepodcast.com/index.php/2019/05/25/interview-with-paul-strack/\" target=\"_blank\"> Page not found &ndash; Mage: The Podcast </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://magethepodcast.com/index.php/2019/05/25/interview-with-paul-strack/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://magethepodcast.com/index.php/2019/05/25/interview-with-paul-strack/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T15:03:33-07:00","id":1392060,"title":"","content":"At 12:58 into the podcast, Paul F. Strack says Awakenings seemed to be pretty random around the world, but the Eurocentric emphasis in the game made it hard not to work with a Eurocentric focus. He was working with what was available at the time and trying to be less Eurocentric with the groups of mages available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13680,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","user":"baakyocalder","date":".  sloppy editing correction 05-27-2020, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T00:58:18-07:00","id":1392145,"title":"","content":"Agreed however since I am only interested in the number of mages in the UK, I can pretty much ignore the implications for the rest of the world. Or, perhaps more satisfyingly I can start with the needs of a eurocentric setting and work outwards from there.<br /> I like the idea of the traditions being eurocentric, but other mage groups filling out the missing numbers in Asia. <br /> Anders number's seem to make sense for Europe, and fit within the (wide) range that Ascensions landscape describes as default.<br /> Actually though, I quite like the idea of using the base symptoms from landscape to account for differences in different places. <br /> Rate of awakenings is a constant. Lifespan should vary across the globe, as should the lethality of the early stages. This might also vary for different groups. <br /> the picture of the UK that is painted by isle of the mighty suggests that Britain is fairly safe for mages. This in turn suggests that if the UK has a default number of mages then the rate of awakening should be low to compensate, which has implications for the wider setting. <br /> it is worth thinking about<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T03:13:36-07:00","id":1392166,"title":"","content":"I love &quot;Isle of the Mighty&quot; and most of my current Chronicles happen in the British Isles, so I would be willing to work in a SV-release (or a C:tD20, one can dream) of an updated &quot;Isle of the Mighty&quot;...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T10:54:25-07:00","id":1392249,"title":"","content":"As a general rule, the number of X in a specific city or region is = &quot;how many do I need for my game?&quot;<br /> <br /> I remember Isle of the Mighty getting a certain amount of flack from British people back in the day. I can't recall specifically why though. <br /> <br /> There's also Dark Ages: Britain, which includes information for Dark Ages: Mage. <br /> <br /> I suspect one could find various ideas from Ars Magica's sourcebooks on the Isles, Heirs to Merlin (England and Wales, what the Order of Hermes used to call the Stonehenge Tribunal), Lion of the North (Scotland, aka the Loch Leglean Tribunal), and The Contested Isle (Ireland, aka the Hibernia Tribunal). I think a lot of the Glastonbury Tor stuff in Isle of the Mighty originated with Ars Magica, IIRC. I suspect there are still Hermetics who think of Europe according to the old tribunal system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T20:30:57-07:00","id":1392406,"title":"","content":"One tiny bit from Heirs to Merlin is the Concordia Covenant, a failed 9th century effort to bring together a number of early factions from House Ex Miscellanea. I could very easily see some idealistic English/British cabal, perhaps in the late Sorcerers Crusade period, the Victorian Era, or post-WW2/early 1st edition period trying to resurrect the name and idea as a Chantry devoted to inter-Tradition cooperation. If nothing else, it'd make a good source of patronage or mentorship for a PC Cabal, as well as a possible reason for them forming. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T01:58:09-07:00","id":1392451,"title":"","content":"Thanks, there are some great ideas there. I will have a look at the ars magica stuff as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T04:47:23-07:00","id":1392478,"title":"","content":"To start with, the first notable thing from isle of the mighty about the British isles is that they are a technocracy stronghold.<br /> the UK is peaceful - no guns, ascension war is low key<br /> since Victoria the technocracy (specifically the NWO) have held defacto control of the British government and authorities<br /> the technocracy are dominated by a small but powerful faction called the harbingers of Avalon<br /> this faction subvert technocracy resources for the glory of Britain (and are probably the power behind brexit)<br /> Birmingham is basically a technocratic fortress","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T05:05:34-07:00","id":1392480,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14453\" data-vbnamecard=\"14453\">Tamuz</a> would the Technocracy also control Handsworth or would that be Nephandi territory?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T07:30:03-07:00","id":1392517,"title":"","content":"It is more the center of Birmingham that is a technocracy strong hold. They seem to have a construct (or constructs) for most conventions sited under and around the city, linked by a network of tunnels. <br /> <br /> next, what makes Britain dark? <br /> 1) inequality. <br /> Britain is essentially stratified into the elite, and the common. <br /> the awakened make up an elite of their own, and even enemies will treat one another with respect, while those below them tend to elicit a mixture of scorn, pity, and indifference. <br /> for sleepers there are the wealthy elite who run the government, own companies and the media, make the rules, and are largely above them. <br /> Within the elite there are the old nobility, who have ties and allegiances going back hundreds of years and the are the new moneyed elite, who might have wealth going back generations but still struggle to get inside the most exclusive clubs. <br /> Within the commoners there are those who work, making up the backbone of Britain's once thriving economy, and those who don't. <br /> geographically there is the elite south where the countries remaining industry and syndicate backers bring progress and prosperity, and there is the common north where whole towns have been plunged into destitution by the loss of old industries such as mining and steel and Entire generations of families languish on sink estates like the infamous chatsworth estate.<br /> <br /> 2) Violence<br /> The ascension war never burned hot in Britain like it did elsewhere, and with strict controls on things like guns the country has a reputation for safety. That reputation is only partly deserved. <br /> If you belong to the elite, you can be confident of a high degree of safety. You have protections from commoners in the form of legal status, wealth, and (including magical for the awakened) power. <br /> for commoners, things are not so simple. Destitution and lack of jobs lead to drug use, gangs, and knife crime. You can always expect respect from those on a similar social level to yourself, but the tharther down the ladder you go, the more brutal that respect becomes. <br /> this is made worse by the fact that elite groups can invariably get away with doing pretty much whatever they like to lower social groups without repercussion.<br /> <br /> 3) Apathy<br /> the technocracy rule Britain with a subtlety that makes them seem like a light hand when in fact they have it in an iron grip. <br /> any tendency for the once proud British people to rebel has been crushed out of them long since. The ruling classes see their privilege as there due, and those not involved directly with the technocracy know not to rock the boat. The working poor think of themselves as well off, living syndicate endorsed lifestyles and directing their scorn and frustration onto those below them. The unworking poor are hooked on subsistence level 'benefits' designed by the syndicate and NWO to keep them quiet and subservient. In return, their existence provides both motivation and vindication to the working poor, who see the comparative rewards of their labour. <br /> <br /> There are probably other factors making the isles dark as well, but I think these set the tone","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T10:44:34-07:00","id":1392597,"title":"","content":"That sounds awful \ud83d\ude22. Do you think a British person who wasn\u2019t part of the elite would be better off moving to a different country?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T11:09:12-07:00","id":1392601,"title":"","content":"That's exactly what it's like. And yes, that's why we got the fuck out as soon as we could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T11:26:51-07:00","id":1392606,"title":"","content":"That the UK is a Technocracy stronghold makes perfect sense to me, in light of the Thatcher era and the corresponding Punk movement. In the mid to late 20th century, it was a huge battleground between &quot;soft authoritarianism&quot; and rebellious counterculture. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Invisibles\" target=\"_blank\">The Invisibles</a> was set partially there for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T12:02:50-07:00","id":1392617,"title":"","content":"I would recommend for the structure that the group working on the 'Isle of the Mighty' update go by region.<br /> <br /> Isle of the Mighty had England, Scotland and Wales. Ireland would require some more work.<br /> <br /> Although there's a brief discussion of the Nephandi in Isle of the Mighty as being able to take advantage of the class-based nature of English society, there's not a lot on the Nephandi. I'd amplify the class tensions and ethnocentrism of the British Isles to figure out the Nephandi factions which would be present.<br /> <br /> Also, Britain isn't the United Kingdom until the Act of Union of 1707, which establishes William and Mary (also a significant early U.S. college located in Virginia) as the recognized monarchs and their line follows. So, definitely consider that although there is a United Kingdom, there are regional variations and fractures.<br /> <br /> One book I found useful in my undergraduate and master's studies in history is Linda Colley's <i>Britons: Forging the Nation</i>, 1707-1837 (Amazon link follows)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Britons-Forging-Nation-1707-1837-Revised/dp/0300152809/ref=sr_1_1?crid=1SETO1MLOWHTG&amp;dchild=1&amp;keywords=britons+forging+the+nation+1707-1837&amp;qid=1590777686&amp;s=books&amp;sprefix=britons%2Caps%2C216&amp;sr=1-1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Britons-Forging-Nation-1707-1837-Revised/dp/0300152809/ref=sr_1_1?crid=1SETO1MLOWHTG&amp;dchild=1&amp;keywords=britons+forging+the+nation+1707-1837&amp;qid=1590777686&amp;s=books&amp;sprefix=britons%2Caps%2C216&amp;sr=1-1\" target=\"_blank\"> Amazon.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Britons-Forging-Nation-1707-1837-Revised/dp/0300152809/ref=sr_1_1?crid=1SETO1MLOWHTG&amp;dchild=1&amp;keywords=britons+forging+the+nation+1707-1837&amp;qid=1590777686&amp;s=books&amp;sprefix=britons%2Caps%2C216&amp;sr=1-1\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.amazon.com/Britons-Forging-Nation-1707-1837-Revised/dp/0300152809/ref=sr_1_1?crid=1SETO1MLOWHTG&amp;dchild=1&amp;keywords=britons+forging+the+nation+1707-1837&amp;qid=1590777686&amp;s=books&amp;sprefix=britons%2Caps%2C216&amp;sr=1-1 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T12:34:58-07:00","id":1392631,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2543_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2543\" data-vbnamecard=\"2543\">Thebian</a> thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T12:45:08-07:00","id":1392637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391759-let-s-populate-the-british-isles?p=1392617#post1392617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Britain isn't the United Kingdom until the Act of Union of 1707, which establishes William and Mary (also a significant early U.S. college located in Virginia) as the recognized monarchs and their line follows. So, definitely consider that although there is a United Kingdom, there are regional variations and fractures.<br /> <br /> One book I found useful in my undergraduate and master's studies in history is Linda Colley's <i>Britons: Forging the Nation</i>, 1707-1837 (Amazon link follows)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Britons-Forging-Nation-1707-1837-Revised/dp/0300152809/ref=sr_1_1?crid=1SETO1MLOWHTG&amp;dchild=1&amp;keywords=britons+forging+the+nation+1707-1837&amp;qid=1590777686&amp;s=books&amp;sprefix=britons%2Caps%2C216&amp;sr=1-1\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.amazon.com/Britons-Forgi...s%2C216&amp;sr=1-1</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, this is very important in any game set in the UK. Here's a broad-strokes overview...<br /> <br /> UK, British, and English are all different things. You'll see them used interchangeably, but they're not at all the same. You'll hear people refer to &quot;a British accent&quot;, for example. That term is so broad as to be meaningless. Someone from the East End of London, or from Llangollen in Wales, or from Inverness in Scotland, or from Durham in north-east England all have British accents. But apart from the fact that they all speak English, they don't really have much in common at all. When people say &quot;he speaks with a British accent,&quot; they usually mean something from down south. The vast majority of the country sounds nothing like that . And there's a compelling argument that people from Northern Ireland don't have British accents at all...<br /> <br /> England, Wales, and Scotland are three separate countries. Together, they make up Great Britain, which is the largest of about 6,000 islands that make up the British Isles (which is only a geographical term, not a political one, although it's controversial because it includes Ireland - see below). Together with Northern Ireland, they make up the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland (which is the proper name for the UK). So a &quot;British accent&quot; would be any one of dozens of accents in England, Scotland, and Wales. An &quot;Irish accent&quot; would be one from Ireland (either Northern Ireland or the Republic of Ireland).<br /> <br /> &quot;Britain&quot; and &quot;British&quot; don't actually refer to anything meaningful at all, other than being shorthand for bits of the above, defined only by context (and some weird Roman stuff that hasn't been relevant for about 1,800 years).<br /> <br /> Ireland is the second-largest of the isles, but it's divided into Northern Ireland (part of the UK) and the Republic of Ireland (not part of the UK). The latter doesn't recognise the term &quot;British Isles&quot; at all, really.<br /> <br /> There's also the British Islands, which is a political term, and refers to the UK, the Isle of Man, Guernsey, and Jersey - but you won't hear it used generally.<br /> <br /> As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13680_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13680\" data-vbnamecard=\"13680\">baakyocalder</a> points out, there very much are regional fractures, many of which have become exacerbated in recent times (and have seen armed conflict as well, with the Troubles being an obvious example). For a Mage game, these divisions are excellent territory for developing in-game factions, adventure seeds, and plot and NPC motivations and personalities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T15:06:34-07:00","id":1392682,"title":"","content":"Some great points being raised. I think focusing on regions is a good idea. Perhaps beginning with England.<br /> <br /> some points for those who think it sounds aweful;<br /> <br /> firstly, this is Britain in the world of darkness, and the bad is wildly exagerated. Clearly real world Britain is a much nicer place. I mean WoD Britain would probably have things like a knighted celebrity who openly abuses children for decades without anyone batting an eyelid, or prime ministers who burn money in front of homeless people and have sex with the carcasses of dead animals, or a government that is willing to sacrifice thousands of lives in the name of the economy and use schoolchildren to carry a virus to do it. Clearly none of that would happen in the real world...<br /> <br /> secondly, the British have mostly been convinced by NWO schemes that not only have they never had it so good, but that they are inherently better than everywhere else as well. Even the jobless poor carry a comforting sense of superiority when comparing themselves to foreigners. Things might be tough, but they are comfortably tough. Some Brits might move abroad but for the most part they probably end up congregating with other ex Pat's in little comunities they make as British as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T15:45:16-07:00","id":1392688,"title":"","content":"The WoD is awful. Any work on this dark mirror of our world needs to have a plausible reflection.<br /> <br /> As for Scotland, I wrote a paper in a college course on nationalism about why the Scots were still part of the United Kingdom. This was in 1994, when there was talk of Scotland becoming its own country. My argument at the time was that the benefits of autonomy (the Kirk and much of the educational system not being the same as in England) and being part of a larger economic unit, the British Commonwealth, outweighed the costs to Scotland. In the World of Darkness, all the regional tensions and differences are worth examining as possible fractures to park supernatural factions in.<br /> <br /> So, a supplemental that expands and updates Isle of the Mighty for Mage (it was mostly a Changeling book) is certainly something I think is worth writing. I'm not the writer for that project--to do it well would require a knowledge of the culture beyond what you can pick up in a few college courses in history.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T16:44:43-07:00","id":1392696,"title":"","content":"The divisions in the UK are fascinating. Even within England you have a north/ south divide which may as well create two different countries (ones with a bitter rivalry going), and neighbouring counties can have vastly different dialects and customs. <br /> I agree that to do such a supplement justice would require a huge depth of knowledge. Here I am willing to settle for something rough and ready, with a balance between providing a framework for a British campaign while remaining as true as possible to both the canon wod, and the British isles of the real world. <br /> <br /> <br /> Next we come on to demographics, and the numbers of awakened present. <br /> How often do mages awaken? This is the one I am least sure about. The default is 1 in 100k to 1 in a million.<br /> How safe is it for new mages? Given the slow burn of the ascension war here, and the gentlemanly respect between willworkers, it seems to me that it should be fairly safe for new mages in the UK so long as they tow the line. Mages who cross lines and act out before being taught the rules might fall afoul of regulations and be taken in by technocratic authorities before they know what's what however.<br /> How long do mages live? Again, with a cold ascension war it seems like mages should be fairly long lived as long as they avoid doing anything stupid, at least in England. Things can be a bit rougher over the border. <br /> <br /> That suggests that unless mages awaken with lower regularity than default then they should be relatively common. 1 mage per 100k is probably a lower bound, and the upper bound is around 1 mage per 10k people.<br /> <br /> this could be reduced by lowering the rate of awakening, but doing so should have implications for other countries. <br /> <br /> assuming these numbers, England would have between 560 and 5600 mages. (With Scotland having 55 to 545 mages and Ireland having 70 to 700 mages)<br /> <br /> I think I am trending towards the lower end of the scale, but many change my mind as I look deeper.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T16:56:23-07:00","id":1392699,"title":"","content":"As far as London goes, I do recommend Ben Judah's <b>This is London</b>. Judah is primarily a foreign correspondent, mainly in Russia, parts of Asia, and North Africa, but in this case he goes fairly deep into modern London and especially its immigrant cultures. It's a pretty interesting look at the subject, and probably fairly useful for thinking about some of the modern subcultures the Traditions and Crafts call home. <br /> <br /> Also, historian Peter Ackroyd has written a number of books about English history, including <b>London: The Biography</b> and <b>London Under</b>. The former is an overview of the city's 2000 years of history with a number of anecdotes and bits of folklore, while the latter is the sometimes bizarre world that exists beneath the city's streets, from ancient catacombs to modern infrastructure. The London book has a companion volume, <i>Thames: A Biography</i>, about the history of the river. Also of potential use is his <b>Queer City</b>, which looks at London's history, from Roman times to modern day, entirely from an LBGT+ perspective. And if you've seen the movie <i>The Limehouse Gollum</i>, it's actually based on one of his fiction novels. <br /> <br /> Martin Latham's <b>Londonopolis</b> is a fun overview of curious bits of historical oddities about the city. He's done a similar book about Kent, <i>Kent's Strangest Tales</i>. <br /> <br /> Finding decent books about London's occult history and legacies is kind of hard. Most tend to focus only on specific time periods in extreme detail, are super spotty and shallow, or are built around really weird conspiracy theories (usually involving the Queen of England being a reptoid alien or something). However, <b>The Book of English Magic</b> by Phillip Carr-Gomm and Richard Heygate isn't bad. <br /> <br /> Fictionwise, Ben Aaronovitch's <b>Rivers of London</b> books are a pretty good modern urban fantasy series. Also Benedict Jacka's <b>Alex Verus</b> series. Then in the realm of the very way out there crazy ideas is Simon Green's <b>Nightside</b> series. And the classic <b>Neverwhere</b> by Neil Gaiman, and China Mieville's <b>Kraken</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T17:07:56-07:00","id":1392701,"title":"","content":"To add some contexts on faction, for england<br /> <br /> going by Anders mix (I have seen other breakdowns but cant find right now)<br /> Traditions = 264 to 2640 mages and around 13 to 130 chantries<br /> Technocracy = 132 to 1320 mages and around 6 to 60 chantries<br /> Nephandi = 66 to 660 mages and around 3 to 30 chantries<br /> marauders = 33 to 330 mages who probably dont have chantries<br /> Orphans = 66 to 660 mages and around 3 to 30 chantries.<br /> <br /> this mix may be different in the isles, but it gives us some numbers to start playing with","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T04:23:47-07:00","id":1394016,"title":"","content":"Canon Chantries in England from Isle of the Mighty:<br /> <br /> London -<br /> NWO technocracy construct and HQ for the Harbingers of Avalon (10 members)<br /> Guilty Pleasures - Club/Chantry run by Ecstatic Acharne, frequented by some Nephandi<br /> Westminster Abey - chorus chantry? maybe just meeting place<br /> <br /> Oxford -<br /> Waltham College - Technocracy (mostly Progenitor) construct including research facilities at nearby Grimsfen<br /> <br /> Cambridge -<br /> Barrow College - Tradition Chantry (mostly hermetic but some ether and adept)<br /> <br /> Windsor -<br /> Controlled by NWO (and seat of the Royal family)<br /> <br /> Canturbury -<br /> Popular with chorus (especially christian elements) - Chantry?<br /> <br /> Bath -<br /> Fellowship hall - Ecstatic Fellowship of Pan chantry<br /> <br /> Birmingham -<br /> Technocratic constructs of all conventions connected by warrens of tunnels. Focus on creating educational programs<br /> <br /> Manchester -<br /> Tapestry - Virtual Adept cyber cafe - chantry or independent?<br /> Crucible of Thig - Hermetic cabal/chantry (linked to a cabal in Diosetep - from the book of chantries)<br /> The Manchester House - haunted house and node for Diosetep (from the book of chantries)<br /> <br /> Stonehenge -<br /> A powerful node for Diosetep.<br /> <br /> <br /> That gives a canon figure of:<br /> 4-7 Tradition Chantries (2 Hermetic, 2 Ecstatic, witha possible 2 chorus and 1 Adept)<br /> 4+ Technocracy constructs, depending on how many operate in Birmingham (2 NWO, 1 Progenitor, plus all in Birmingham)<br /> <br /> This clearly leaves room for more (perhaps many more) chantries to operate. Even the lowest guestimate for the number of tradition chantries would give another 6 that have been unacounted for.<br /> Does anybody know of any other canon chantries operating in the UK?<br /> <br /> I find the relative number of canon ecstatic chantries to be surprisingly high, and one notable absence are the Verbena. I think they should at a minimum have a chantry in the New Forest (the birthplace of modern Wicca).<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T08:44:51-07:00","id":1394050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tamuz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391759-let-s-populate-the-british-isles?p=1394016#post1394016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anybody know of any other canon chantries operating in the UK?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hollow One book details a chantry outside Wells in Somerset.<br /> According the Orphan's Survival Guide the Hollowers also have a place in London called Guilty Pleasures, Hazelton Manoron its outskirts and Gethsemone Garden in Scotland. Don't know to what extent these are considered chantries, depends on definition I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T08:44:51-07:00","id":1394051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tamuz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391759-let-s-populate-the-british-isles?p=1394016#post1394016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anybody know of any other canon chantries operating in the UK?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hollow One book details a chantry outside Wells in Somerset.<br /> According the Orphan's Survival Guide the Hollowers also have a place in London called Guilty Pleasures, Hazelton Manoron its outskirts and Gethsemone Garden in Scotland. Don't know to what extent these are considered chantries, depends on definition I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T16:34:20-07:00","id":1394181,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I whil add those in.<br /> Isle of the mighty doesnt give much clarity on what is a chantry and what is just a line canal either in most places. For these purposes I am seeing a chantry as a collective of multiple cabals sharing a location or purpose. I am also willing to play loose with canon by expanding and splitting canon cabals if and where it makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T18:19:03-07:00","id":1394203,"title":"","content":"A minor note: <b>Isle of the Mighty</b> says that the Harbingers of Avalon are just ten people; but <b>M20</b> updates that to say that their ranks have swelled over time. That is, the original material is now out of date. That said, it's entirely possible that this is a case where this particular Chantry hasn't changed much; but where the Harbingers originally consisted solely of this Chantry, it is now \u201cmerely\u201d the first of many Chantries under the banner of the Harbingers of Avalon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T06:01:21-07:00","id":1394309,"title":"","content":"Thanks. That is an interesting note. By their nature, the Harbingers of Avalon must all be british (or working abroad for british interests) so even if they have spread to other chantries those chantries should probably be british. I can see them keeping a HQ in london with other local branches operating across the isles.<br /> It is also interestng because it makes the point that time has moved on since the snapshot captured by Isles of the mighty. Things have probably changed for other factions as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T06:30:22-07:00","id":1394317,"title":"","content":"Actually, no; they're <i>not</i> all British anymore, and their influence has extended well beyond the isles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T07:39:07-07:00","id":1394561,"title":"","content":"Interesting. I will have to look that up","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T23:27:39-07:00","id":1394727,"title":"","content":"This page has some interesting information - it seems like the author has dug through every official oWoD book to get some numbers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038344-the-demographics-of-mage\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038344-the-demographics-of-mage\"> The Demographics of Mage - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038344-the-demographics-of-mage\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1038344-the-demographics-of-mage </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> These charts include only canonical mages, and include unnamed magi, but should contain 95 - 99% of all mentioned mages in the oWoD. Where appropriate, quoted </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Or they're just pulling #'s out their ass.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T19:09:07-07:00","id":1396274,"title":"","content":"One of the things I have used in my own games is Woodwich Downs, the estate of an ennobled Gardeners of the Tree family since the Tudor era. Among its grounds is what used to be the Old Faith stronghold that Nightshade came from, which was destroyed during Wyndgarde's March and rebuilt under the owners. I usually have it in Gloucestershire.<br /> <br /> Also of potential interest, the town of Boscastle in Cornwall, home to the Museum of Witchcraft and Magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 06-14-2020, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T11:59:16-07:00","id":1396437,"title":"","content":"Isle of the Mighty was just discussed on Mage: The Podcast. It reminded me of my impression of the book--a book for Changeling with just a little Mage stuff thrown in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://magethepodcast.com/index.php/2020/06/13/tomes-of-magick-isle-of-the-mighty/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://magethepodcast.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/cropped-test.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://magethepodcast.com/index.php/2020/06/13/tomes-of-magick-isle-of-the-mighty/\" target=\"_blank\"> Page not found &ndash; Mage: The Podcast </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://magethepodcast.com/index.php/2020/06/13/tomes-of-magick-isle-of-the-mighty/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://magethepodcast.com/index.php/2020/06/13/tomes-of-magick-isle-of-the-mighty/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T10:46:11-07:00","id":1398383,"title":"","content":"A few years ago, I ran a London centric mage game. I wrote it all up as I went along and came up with the following bits of world-building<br /> <br /> The Verbena featured heavily in my campaign, mostly because two of the players wanted to be verbena and another had verbena as a main factor of their backstory. The Verbena book, funnily enough has quite a bit of information, such as the Glastonbury circle who are looking for the return of King Arthur<br /> <br /> I had London as a technocratic stronghold. The Progenitors headquarters was in Guy's hospital, the Syndicate practically owned the City of London, but had a major presence pretty much everywhere. the NWO was essentially the civil service of parliament and the operators of MI5, that didn't really come up much in the campaign though. What did come up was that there was a huge Void Engineer base underneath Greenwich. I didn't feature the Iterator's in my campaign so I hadn't done much research to consider suitable hold ups.<br /> <br /> I had a single Verbena group operating in the very epicentre of London. These are the titular Keepers of the Wyck, they ordained to keep their ways alive, defending sacred locations such as Hampstead Heath from falling to the hands of technocratic sanitation.<br /> <br /> On the Tradition side of things. The major presence within the city was the Celestial Chorus, the Hermetics, and the Euthanatos, who had taken it upon themselves to manage the London Tribunal. When House Quaesitori identified members form outside of the Order as having committed a serious crime, such as the harbouring of a widderslainte, members of the three order would set up a tribunal in order to hear the accusations, pass judgement, and ensure that any threats to the traditions themselves were managed appropriately.<br /> <br /> Most Verbena groups steered clear of London due to the heavy technocratic presence having weakened so many of the links they rely upon to commune, but as long as the Keepers keep the practice alive, they know they can seek aid and shelter if they may ever have need to enter the city.<br /> <br /> The Hermetics will have a number of members from house Jerbiton in various different institutions around London, from museums to universities, in order to keep a look out for potential recruits to bring into the folds. The Order had a fairly well kept chantry in which a number of important hermetic leaders would congregate to discuss and share their teachings.<br /> <br /> I still have the link to my campaign write-ups in my description if you wanted to dive into that for more inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}